  "jcr:description": "Reprocessing of single-use medical devices (SUDs) is the practice of inspecting, cleaning, function testing, packaging and sterilizing so that they can be clinically and safely used again. Reprocessing of SUDs is regulated by the FDA. We satisfy all FDA regulatory requirements to reprocess medical devices and ensure that our reprocessed devices are substantially equivalent to original equipment devices.",
